      "math_academy_id": "e-6282",
      "problem": "Find the coordinates of the vector $\\mathbf{x}$ relative to the basis $\\mathcal{B}=\\{ \\mathbf{b}_1, \\mathbf{b}_2 \\},$ where\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14274696/assets/a6fe35404846f3ba97ea83a95ebbcffae29088d415f0893e237cc1a92ee94cfe.svg)",
      "worked_solution": "Remember, the order of the vectors in a basis is important.\n\nNotice that \n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14274696/assets/b8de901e06baeedda03c6bfe461a0f9e92cd28c16d723bca80e535646604e7dc.svg)\n\nwhich means that\n\n$$\n\\mathbf{x} = (-5) \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_1 + 2 \\cdot \\mathbf{b}_2\n$$\n\nand therefore\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/differential/14274696/assets/f1c8c4137bd63c497c5dc6571b94f76a712832b9ff0d24d404680d529a0c8222.svg)",
